Q37: What is LoRa, briefly?
---
LoRa (Long Range) is a low-power, long-range, unlicensed, and non-line-of-sight wireless communication technology. It is primarily used for IoT (Internet of Things) applications, allowing devices to transmit small amounts of data over long distances (kilometers) while consuming very little power, often running on batteries for years. It operates in the sub-GHz frequency bands and is known for its robustness against interference and its ability to penetrate obstacles.<|im_end|>
